e572e142edf8c86d74b155a90dd247d","position":"1787888673309866001-3002a20f-ba5b-4b2f-9fbe-86df650d4faa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9343933f4214de2149fbd89628c5d2bfea37c19fcaa232e3849056d26d6f3bd1","event_uuid":"3d38ab8d-b835-4837-9b73-b7f8b778255a","position":{"commit_sha":"b03682a0aaeabd3be6b18f82366d66ba17a0a8e9","position":"1787889271818436001-3d38ab8d-b835-4837-9b73-b7f8b778255a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5d916c8ba63b7bd5c8a489b10dea8e71530ea056b1cf0631818ea622d835c1da","event_uuid":"bbf56283-635f-433d-be22-cccd4c7f1a12","position":{"commit_sha":"1e2192e14c073fc1fdbc7ee65247f079eb8db1d1","position":"1787890110573950537-bbf56283-635f-433d-be22-cccd4c7f1a12"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787866425773177652,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a4b2ad90-076a-40cd-87f4-2a10188a0650","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"},{"link_uuid":"bbf56283-635f-433d-be22-cccd4c7f1a12","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8c5d-215e-8b48-4137"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nCLI users need to see the cross-session warning inline. rebar already has a stderr\n`WARN:`/`WARNING:` convention that leaves stdout and exit codes untouched\n(`src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:99` `warn_secret_screen_refused`; the fsck `WARN:` lines in\n`src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py`). This story emits that warning for CLI commands that\ntarget **one specific ticket**, and — per the brainstorm scope — **never** for bulk reads\n(`list` / `search` / `ready` / `next-batch`).\n\nDepends on the detector (`cross_session_warning_for`, sibling story) and on the reducer\nclearing (so a non-`in_progress` ticket has no holder and never warns).\n\n## Approach\n\nDefine the single-ticket-targeted CLI command set as an **explicit, data-driven\nallowlist** (a frozenset in the CLI dispatch layer) rather than inferring it, so bulk-read\ncommands are excluded by construction. The set covers single-ticket reads and mutations,\nusing the exact command spellings registered in `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`'s\n`_CORE_FACTORIES`: `show`, `comment`, `edit`, `transition`, `reopen`, `tag`, `untag`,\n`set-file-impact`, `deps`, `archive`, `check-ac`, `clarity-check`, `link`,\n`unlink`. (There is no separate `declare-no-file-impact` CLI command — the no-impact form\nis `set-file-impact <id> --none`, already covered by `set-file-impact`.) It excludes\n`list`, `search`, `ready`, `next-batch`, and `create` (no\npre-existing target). For `link` / `unlink` (two endpoints) the warning is computed for the\n**primary** ticket argument (`id1`) only.\n\nAt the point where each allowlisted single-ticket CLI command has resolved its ticket id,\ncall `cross_session_warning_for(ticket_id, repo_root=...)`; when it\nreturns a string, `sys.stderr.write(\"WARN: \" + msg + \"\\n\")` **before** performing the\noperation, so the warning is visible even if the op itself is quiet. stdout content and the\nprocess exit code are unchanged. `claim` is intentionally **not** in the set: claiming an\n`in_progress` ticket already fails with `ConcurrencyError`/exit 10 before any warning path\n(`docs/concurrency.md`).\n\nThe emit is **best-effort and must never break the command**: `cross_session_warning_for`\nperforms a state read, so wrap it so that any exception it raises (corrupt/absent/locked\nstate) is swallowed and the command proceeds unwarned — the warning is advisory, never a\ngate on the underlying operation. The gate that decides whether to emit is the **allowlist\nfrozenset keyed by the resolved command name**, evaluated at the dispatch layer — not a\nsingle shared id-resolution helper. `require_id` (`src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:157`) is\nonly *one* of the id-resolution paths (some reads such as `show`/`deps` and the gate\ncommands resolve their id on their own arm), so the implementation confirms each\nallowlisted command's resolved-id point during implementation and emits there; the frozenset\nmembership check — not a `require_id` call — is what excludes bulk commands.\n\nThe warning is computed from the ticket state **at operation time** (before a mutation\napplies), so e.g. a `transition <id> in_progress closed` run by another session warns about\nholder A and *then* clears the provenance — the read precedes the write.\n\n## Scope\n\n- The CLI dispatch layer under `src/rebar/_cli/` — define the allowlist frozenset (keyed by\n  the command spellings in `_registry.py`'s `_CORE_FACTORIES`) and add the stderr emit at\n  each allowlisted command's resolved-id point (which may be `require_id`,\n  `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:157`, or a command's own id-resolution arm). Confirm the\n  exact per-command insertion point by reading the dispatch during implementation; the\n  allowlist frozenset is the single source of \"which commands warn\".\n- `docs/user-guide.md` — a short note that single-ticket CLI commands warn on stderr when\n  another session holds the ticket, and that bulk commands do not.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **real CLI subprocess + persisted-state assertion** (test-design §3 \"CLI parsing,\nstreams, env, exit codes\" — the mechanism crosses argv parsing, env-var session resolution,\nand stderr). Use a real temporary tracker; set `REBAR_SESSION_ID` per invocation to model\ndistinct sessions.\n\n- Claim a ticket with `REBAR_SESSION_ID=A` (so `claimed_session=A`). Run `rebar show <id>`\n  and `rebar comment <id> \"x\"` with `REBAR_SESSION_ID=B`: assert **stderr** contains `WARN:`\n  and the holder id `A`, stdout is the normal output, and exit code is `0`.\n- Negative control (same session): the same commands with `REBAR_SESSION_ID=A` emit **no**\n  `WARN:` line (exit 0).\n- Bulk exclusion: `rebar list` (and `rebar ready`) with `REBAR_SESSION_ID=B` emit **no**\n  `WARN:` line even though the store contains A's `in_progress` ticket.\n- Unset-id silence: `rebar show <id>` with `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset emits no `WARN:` line.\n- `link` primary-endpoint: `rebar link <id1> <id2> ...` as session B, with A holding `id1`,\n  emits a single `WARN:` naming holder `A` computed for the **primary** `id1` (not `id2`).\n- Defect-seeded: temporarily point the emit at the wrong ticket / drop the allowlist guard\n  and show the bulk-exclusion and holder-id assertions go RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] With ticket held by session A, `rebar show <id>` and `rebar comment <id> ...` run as\n  session B print a `WARN:` line naming holder `A` to **stderr**, with unchanged stdout and\n  exit code 0 (checked by a CLI subprocess test under `make test`).\n- [x] Negative control: the same commands as session A print no `WARN:` line (checked by the\n  same test asserting stderr has no `WARN:`).\n- [x] `rebar list` and `rebar ready` as session B print no cross-session `WARN:` line even\n  with A's `in_progress` ticket present (checked by a bulk-exclusion assertion).\n- [x] `rebar show <id>` with `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset prints no `WARN:` line (checked by an\n  unset-id assertion).\n- [x] `rebar link <id1> <id2>` as session B, with A holding `id1`, prints a single `WARN:`\n  naming holder `A` computed for the **primary** `id1` only (checked by a link\n  primary-endpoint assertion in the CLI subprocess test).\n- [x] The stderr emit is best-effort: when `cross_session_warning_for` raises (corrupt /\n  absent / locked state), the command still completes normally and unwarned — the warning\n  never gates the underlying operation (checked by a test that forces the detector to raise\n  and asserts the command's exit code and stdout are unchanged with no `WARN:` line).\n- [x] `docs/user-guide.md` documents the CLI stderr warning and the bulk exclusion (checked:\n  `grep -n \"another session\" docs/user-guide.md` matches).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py","reason":"single dispatch choke point: allowlist frozenset + best-effort stderr WARN emit for single-ticket commands (excludes bulk + claim)"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document the CLI stderr cross-session warning, bulk exclusion, and warnings.cross_session toggle"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cross_session_cli.py","reason":"CLI-surface oracle: real python -m rebar subprocess tests (warn/suppress matrix, link primary-endpoint, config toggle, best-effort)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"],["parent","1aca-695f-a0a4-4236"],["relates_to","8c5d-215e-8b48-4137"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1aca-695f-a0a4-4236","parent_status_uuid":"71d92041-555c-4fc8-9186-ecaef4453887","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5d55-15ab-8ec1-4622","ticket_type":"story","title":"CLI: emit cross-session WARN on stderr for single-ticket commands","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d187b69b-e21d-4fa1-bb98-e8537c54a8ca","857c35f7-c621-40e